  "sourceData": {
    "answer": "to: go-around | return | surround | concern-(usu.-of-disputes)",
    "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an <ja>う</ja> sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means <kanji>patrol</kanji>, but what do you do when you patrol? You go around, which is <vocabulary>to go around</vocabulary>.",
    "readingMnemonic": "You're going around patrolling to protect the house of <reading>Meg</reading> (<ja>めぐ</ja>) Ryan. Just imagine Meg Ryan's house, and you walking around it. Imagine Meg Ryan looking out at you."
